# a-sweep-that-fails

The collections service is down, so the case runs out of patience — and one of the sweeper's 
own units of work does not commit: it rolls back, having selected and charged nothing, or it 
commits and the process dies before the re-commands and the verdict leave the outbox. The 
clock moved either way. 

search: exhaustive — every schedule this transport allows was walked
distinct end states: 4

[A]
    identity was told: [PORTAL_PURGE_FAILED]
    the parts confirmed: {alice/comments=1, alice/memes=1}
    still on the wire: [content-commands→collections PURGE_USER_CONTENT → collections, content-commands→collections PURGE_USER_CONTENT → collections, content-commands→collections PURGE_USER_CONTENT → collections, content-commands→collections PURGE_USER_CONTENT → collections, content-commands→collections RESTORE_USER_CONTENT → collections]
    rows:
      meme alice's meme by alice
      comment alice's own comment under somebody's meme by alice

